  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "There's already a request for a convenient way for world creators to choose to add footsteps to their world, but really it would be ideal if all worlds gained footsteps automatically, by default. (World creators could still customize their footsteps per surface if they want, but a world with none set should still use a default set until custom ones are set.) It's so startling to have someone come up behind you without any warning -- I don't even mean people who are deliberately trolling, just people who are trying to be friendly and haven't realised that you haven't seen them yet. Hearing people coming and going, having any clue about the presence of other users nearby around corners, would add so much to a sense of social presence in these currently eerily silent worlds.",
